    "soak": "256 MiB, 8 lanes, 200 ms TTFB, 2 MiB playable priming; three rates with memory/FileRangeStore/SimpleCache, nine cases; late concurrency measured beyond two seconds of playback",
    "cacheImplementations": "matrix disk mode uses the real filesystem FileRangeStore adapter; actual production DiskPrefetcher/PlaybackDiskCache/SimpleCache separately tested on Robolectric API23, including all three high-bitrate cases and protocol/cache edge cases",
    "eligibility": "LoadControl demand=true, not EOF, scheduled end before consumed position+window, and room for another full chunk allocation; sustained concurrency assertion applies to uncached memory mode. Cached bytes can legitimately reduce network work.",
    "meanActiveTcp": "5 ms samples across entire playback, including EOF drain and full-window idle; less TCP occupancy can reflect reduced HTTP overhead and a filled forward window",
    "integrity": "Every final case compares delivered SHA-256 against the source, checks received byte count, unique requested starts, lane cap and measured payload+disk copies against the production StreamPolicy budget. The soak additionally verifies independently recorded HTTP interval non-overlap and late concurrency.",
